{"t": 159.536, "n": 126, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I wrote the plan to `plugins/tempergraph/docs/plans/i21b.plan.md` with status `planned`. I did not run anything. I opened `plan.rule.md` and `documents.rule.md` with the read tool first.\n\n- **Complexity:** `complex`. The rows would touch about 11 files (the limit for `simple` is 10), and the work needs 5 phases and more than 12 rows. So the plan carries phases, goals, weights and the three verification commands only. The expand step writes the rows and the proof table.\n- **Requirements:** R1 to R7 cover AC 1 to AC 6. Each cites spec ids from ECC-B13 and ECC-B21 to ECC-B24, with ECC-AC14 and ECC-AC16 to ECC-AC19, and from LIF-B10, LIF-B17 and LIF-AC12.\n- **Phases:**\n  1. Refuse a CLI without `--strict-mcp-config` through the probe's existing `probe_failed` reason, and make the stand-in `claude` list the flag.\n  2. Refuse undefined declared servers at preflight through an optional executor method.\n  3. Make the launch fail naming the server, and change the three tests that pinned the silent launch.\n  4. Make the live probe read every turn through an offline-testable helper.\n  5. Fix the runbook rows and the compatibility record.\n- **Docs to update:** `plugins/tempergraph/docs/plans/live-checks.plan.md`, for the L-43 row, its result row and the lead of section 4.\n- **Reading list:** I started from the hand-off's list. Section 0 names the extra files I opened and why: `runner.py`, `cli/main.py`, `contracts.py`, `standins.py` and `tempergraph.commands.json`.\n\nJudgement calls and risks:\n- **Offline proof for AC 1:** the live test is skipped without `TEMPERGRAPH_LIVE=1`, so the proof of AC 1 has to be an offline test of the helper. The plan says so in section 0.\n- **Preflight working folder:** preflight has no working folder today. The plan reads from the folder the command runs in. A server defined only in the worktree's local scope would then fail at launch under ECC-B23, not at preflight.\n- **Context threshold:** I put a 30,000-token threshold in the Phase 4 goal. No spec sets it, and it comes from the operator's figures.\n- **Spec size:** `executor-claude-code.spec.md` has 571 bytes of room, so the plan edits no spec.\n- **Open question from the hand-off:** I took its default `a`, which widens `range` to `>=2.1.329,<=2.1.332`.\n- **Previous review's note:** ECC-B13's sentence is still over 500 characters from before this task. A plan can't edit a spec, so I only recorded it in section 0.\n\nARTIFACT plan: plugins/tempergraph/docs/plans/i21b.plan.md\nARTIFACT complexity: complex", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "69875a80-b5aa-4941-9737-770872c15823"}
